155
00:09:25,679 --> 00:09:26,519
What is it?

156
00:09:26,879 --> 00:09:28,000
The smell of defeat.

157
00:09:28,279 --> 00:09:29,879
Alright, stop dawdling.

158
00:09:29,879 --> 00:09:31,360
Reflect and review.

159
00:09:31,360 --> 00:09:32,120
Who

160
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:34,440
made the biggest mistake today?

161
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:37,000
Don't look around. It's you, Lin Qingyuan.

162
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:38,919
You insisted on shooting at a critical moment,

163
00:09:38,919 --> 00:09:40,440
wasting many opportunities to turn the tables.

164
00:09:41,039 --> 00:09:41,840
Li Haoyu,

165
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:43,919
you made many mistakes and fouls.

166
00:09:43,919 --> 00:09:45,080
You are too hasty.

167
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:48,279
Zhou Yang, are you so tired?

168
00:09:48,279 --> 00:09:49,840
You are not active enough.

169
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:51,279
Gu Chenyang, you are the same.

170
00:09:51,279 --> 00:09:53,399
The more behind you are, the more you think.

171
00:09:53,399 --> 00:09:54,840
You are hesitant to shoot.

172
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:55,840
Xu Anbo.

173
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:00,240
Where's Xu Anbo?

174
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:02,399
He had something at the boxing gym.

175
00:10:02,639 --> 00:10:04,960
He and Chi Jia left early.

176
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:07,879
Look.

177
00:10:07,879 --> 00:10:08,600
Look.

178
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,519
Running away after losing a game.

179
00:10:10,519 --> 00:10:11,879
What kind of team is this?

180
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:12,879
Coach.

181
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:14,600
Today...

182
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:15,960
It wasn't that bad.

183
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:16,919
Yeah.

184
00:10:17,279 --> 00:10:19,000
I didn't do well today,

185
00:10:19,399 --> 00:10:20,120
but others

186
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:21,720
did well.

187
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:23,879
Coach,

188
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:26,519
Fanghe No. 3 Middle School is indeed strong.

189
00:10:26,519 --> 00:10:27,879
We lost today

190
00:10:27,879 --> 00:10:29,159
and made many mistakes,

191
00:10:29,159 --> 00:10:30,360
but I think

192
00:10:30,919 --> 00:10:31,960
our performance

193
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:33,360
wasn't that bad.

194
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:34,559
Yeah, coach.

195
00:10:34,559 --> 00:10:35,240
Yeah.

196
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:38,240
Do you think so?

197
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:43,159
That's right.

198
00:10:43,679 --> 00:10:44,720
Why do you

199
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:45,799
look so upset?

200
00:10:45,799 --> 00:10:47,320
Why the long faces?

201
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:50,799
Winning and losing are common in games.

202
00:10:51,039 --> 00:10:52,159
Fanghe No.3 Middle School

203
00:10:52,159 --> 00:10:53,120
is the team

204
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:54,159
that fouls the most.

205
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:55,559
You guys were obviously

206
00:10:55,559 --> 00:10:56,799
disturbed today.

207
00:10:56,799 --> 00:10:57,720
But none of you

208
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:59,360
were injured.

209
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:00,159
That should be

210
00:11:00,159 --> 00:11:01,519
the most gratifying thing.

211
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:03,120
So,

212
00:11:03,399 --> 00:11:04,840
cheer up.

213
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:06,919
The game isn't over yet.

214
00:11:07,159 --> 00:11:08,120
Let's

215
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:09,559
keep working hard.

216
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:11,879
Good, you all know how to answer quickly.

217
00:11:11,879 --> 00:11:12,399
Okay.

218
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:13,639
Go home early.

219
00:11:15,039 --> 00:11:16,759
Goodbye, coach.

220
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:21,639
As your supervisor,

221
00:11:21,639 --> 00:11:22,440
I need to remind you

222
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:23,519
of something.

223
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:24,759
What?

224
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:26,240
Check the group chat.

225
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:36,360
According to the latest

226
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:38,000
club management rules,

227
00:11:38,399 --> 00:11:40,600
if a club member fails

228
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:42,600
two or more exams,

229
00:11:42,840 --> 00:11:43,799
or

230
00:11:44,320 --> 00:11:46,320
ranks in the bottom

231
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:47,480
10%,

232
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,039
they'll be forced to

233
00:11:50,039 --> 00:11:51,879
pause club activities for a month.

234
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:54,039
I've checked.

235
00:11:54,519 --> 00:11:55,679
Lin Qingyuan, Li Haoyu,

236
00:11:56,039 --> 00:11:57,639
your scores in the last two monthly exams

237
00:11:57,639 --> 00:11:59,360
were both in the bottom 10% of your grade.

238
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:00,759
To be exact,

239
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:02,559
the bottom 5%.

240
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:05,240
That means

241
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:06,639
if they don't improve

242
00:12:06,639 --> 00:12:08,480
in this midterm,

243
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:10,240
they won't be able to participate

244
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:11,159
in the following group matches.

245
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:12,519
What do you think?

246
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,159
What should we do?

247
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Who can help us?

248
00:12:40,559 --> 00:12:41,919
For the first function problem,

249
00:12:41,919 --> 00:12:42,639
you can first look at

250
00:12:42,639 --> 00:12:43,759
the AI's approach to solving it.

251
00:12:43,879 --> 00:12:45,240
It's explained very clearly.

252
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:48,720
What's wrong?

253
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:50,600
Take a look for yourself.

254
00:12:53,279 --> 00:12:54,720
Why are there so many words?

255
00:12:54,919 --> 00:12:56,600
I didn't ask it to give you the answer,

256
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:57,399
but to use

257
00:12:57,399 --> 00:12:58,679
Socratic method.

258
00:12:58,679 --> 00:12:59,799
Starting from the question,

259
00:12:59,799 --> 00:13:01,080
it guides you step by step

260
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:03,360
to analyze the problem, retrieve knowledge,

261
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:04,440
and solve the problem.

262
00:13:04,799 --> 00:13:05,720
In this way,

263
00:13:05,720 --> 00:13:06,720
you will not only learn

264
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:07,840
this question,

265
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:08,480
but you can handle

266
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:10,000
the whole type of questions.

267
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,320
This is called teaching a man to fish

268
00:13:12,320 --> 00:13:14,399
instead of giving him a fish.

269
00:13:15,679 --> 00:13:16,679
Orcs

270
00:13:17,519 --> 00:13:18,919
are never slaves, right?

271
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:20,360
You just mentioned

272
00:13:20,360 --> 00:13:22,000
Socrates.

273
00:13:22,879 --> 00:13:23,399
Which game's hero

274
00:13:23,399 --> 00:13:24,600
is he?

275
00:13:27,519 --> 00:13:28,360
Ten minutes.

276
00:13:28,799 --> 00:13:29,679
After watching,

277
00:13:29,679 --> 00:13:31,120
I'll give you a similar question.

278
00:13:31,120 --> 00:13:32,080
If you can't solve it,

279
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:32,919
you'll be penalized with five more.

280
00:13:39,399 --> 00:13:40,679
Mr. Gu,

281
00:13:40,679 --> 00:13:41,679
we have a question.

282
00:13:42,399 --> 00:13:44,320
When is Mr. Zhou Yang coming?

283
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:46,840
Hello, Director Qian.

284
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:47,519
Hello.

285
00:13:48,879 --> 00:13:49,879
Professor Lin,

286
00:13:49,879 --> 00:13:51,519
thank you for coming today.

287
00:13:52,159 --> 00:13:54,320
Your lecture on the Reading Week

288
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:55,440
was truly fantastic.

289
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:57,399
Director Qian, you're too kind.

290
00:13:57,399 --> 00:13:59,200
This is mainly due to the national advocacy

291
00:13:59,200 --> 00:14:00,639
and the school's support.

292
00:14:00,639 --> 00:14:01,519
The Parent Committee

293
00:14:01,519 --> 00:14:03,039
just played a small role.

294
00:14:03,919 --> 00:14:04,799
Professor Lin,

295
00:14:04,799 --> 00:14:06,279
you're too modest.

296
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:09,720
This year, we're just trying it out on our own.

297
00:14:10,399 --> 00:14:12,320
Next year, for the National Reading Week,

298
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:13,120
Professor Lin,

299
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:14,720
we'll need your continued support.

300
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:16,120
I'll do my best to support it.

301
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:17,120
Thank you, thank you.

302
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:17,639
You're welcome.

303
00:14:17,639 --> 00:14:18,399
Hello, Director Qian.

304
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:21,320
This young man,

305
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:22,840
are you from the Basketball Club?

306
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:25,559
Yes, ma'am. And who might you be?

307
00:14:25,559 --> 00:14:27,000
Let me introduce.

308
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:27,639
This is

309
00:14:27,639 --> 00:14:29,159
Gu Chenyang's mother,

310
00:14:29,159 --> 00:14:30,480
Professor Lin Ruoyun.

311
00:14:30,720 --> 00:14:31,559
Hello.

312
00:14:31,559 --> 00:14:32,320
Hello, ma'am.

313
00:14:32,759 --> 00:14:34,120
He's the president

314
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:35,240
of our Yibei Student Union,

315
00:14:35,559 --> 00:14:36,840
Zhou...

316
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:38,039
Zhou Yang.

317
00:14:38,399 --> 00:14:39,159
[Zhou Yang,]

318
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:40,759
[you finally]

319
00:14:40,759 --> 00:14:42,440
[found us!]

320
00:14:42,440 --> 00:14:43,799
[Zhou Yang, help us!]

321
00:14:43,799 --> 00:14:44,039
What's going on?

322
00:14:44,039 --> 00:14:44,879
Don't let Gu Chenyang

323
00:14:44,879 --> 00:14:45,799
tutor us!

324
00:14:45,799 --> 00:14:47,279
We're too far apart in intelligence.

325
00:14:47,279 --> 00:14:49,840
It's like we're torturing each other!

326
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:52,679
Director.

327
00:14:55,879 --> 00:14:57,360
Aunt Lin.

328
00:14:58,120 --> 00:14:59,879
Long time no see, Haoyu.

329
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:07,600
Aunt, don't give it to him.

330
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:08,679
He can't even understand it.

331
00:15:08,679 --> 00:15:09,159
You give it to him.

332
00:15:09,159 --> 00:15:10,320
I can understand it.

333
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:11,360
Who says I can't?

334
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:12,799
Can you understand this?

335
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:14,399
Of course I can.

336
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:16,480
They're so lively.

337
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,360
This book, The Old Man and the Sea,

338
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:18,960
is for you.

339
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:19,759
Mom.

340
00:15:19,759 --> 00:15:20,159
Thank you, auntie.

341
00:15:20,159 --> 00:15:21,120
I know you like it.

342
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:22,240
Chen Yang is here.

343
00:15:22,879 --> 00:15:23,480
He's here.

344
00:15:25,440 --> 00:15:25,960
Come here.

345
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:26,679
Come and sit.

346
00:15:28,480 --> 00:15:30,240
I'm giving out books to everyone.

347
00:15:30,519 --> 00:15:31,799
Today at your school,

348
00:15:31,799 --> 00:15:33,000
there was a promotion

349
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,120
of Reading Week.

350
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:35,080
Reading Week?

351
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:37,080
Yes, after the midterms,

352
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:38,639
the school will fully implement it.

353
00:15:38,879 --> 00:15:40,600
From now on, everyone must read a book

354
00:15:40,919 --> 00:15:42,480
in the first week of every month

355
00:15:42,879 --> 00:15:44,200
and complete a reading report.

356
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:47,840
Why are there

357
00:15:48,039 --> 00:15:49,600
so many tasks from the school?

358
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:51,279
It's hard to be a student,

359
00:15:51,559 --> 00:15:53,240
and it's even harder to be

360
00:15:53,240 --> 00:15:54,879
a good student.

361
00:15:55,759 --> 00:15:57,039
With your grades,

362
00:15:57,039 --> 00:15:58,799
do you really think you're good students?

363
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:02,159
Chen Yang,

364
00:16:02,480 --> 00:16:04,840
everyone has their strengths.

365
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:06,399
Good students can be

366
00:16:06,399 --> 00:16:08,080
defined in different ways.

367
00:16:08,519 --> 00:16:11,200
Look at Xiaolin and Haoyu,

368
00:16:11,600 --> 00:16:12,919
one is enthusiastic,

369
00:16:12,919 --> 00:16:14,039
the other is loyal.

370
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:16,080
They're both good students, right?

371
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:17,840
Right.

372
00:16:18,399 --> 00:16:21,360
But, you still need to study.

373
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:23,120
In our family,

374
00:16:23,559 --> 00:16:24,519
Chenyang reads

375
00:16:24,519 --> 00:16:26,000
two books a month.

376
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,679
He's been doing this for years.

377
00:16:29,679 --> 00:16:31,600
Who would've thought?

378
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,639
That's the gap

379
00:16:33,639 --> 00:16:35,159
between people.

380
00:16:36,279 --> 00:16:36,960
Zhou Yang,

381
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:38,039
do you remember

382
00:16:38,039 --> 00:16:39,080
our agreement?

383
00:16:39,360 --> 00:16:40,159
I remember.

384
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:42,240
I'll help you catch up next week

385
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:44,159
and lighten Gu Chenyang's load.

386
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:46,919
Alright,

387
00:16:46,919 --> 00:16:49,159
enough about studying.

388
00:16:49,159 --> 00:16:50,679
Today, I'm treating.

389
00:16:50,679 --> 00:16:52,000
Whoever eats the most

390
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,320
and enjoys the most

391
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:54,360
will be my

392
00:16:54,360 --> 00:16:55,600
favorite student.

393
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:56,240
Okay?

394
00:16:56,240 --> 00:16:56,799
Okay!

395
00:16:56,799 --> 00:16:57,600
Let's eat!

396
00:17:16,880 --> 00:17:18,160
Son, have some fruit.

397
00:17:20,119 --> 00:17:21,039
What are you reading?

398
00:17:22,680 --> 00:17:24,680
The Alchemist.

399
00:17:26,079 --> 00:17:27,519
Why did you choose this one?

400
00:17:28,039 --> 00:17:28,759
It's the first book

401
00:17:28,759 --> 00:17:30,440
on the Reading Week recommendation list.

402
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:31,480
I want to finish

403
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:32,400
all the books this semester.

404
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:36,319
I thought

405
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:37,440
you were interested

406
00:17:37,440 --> 00:17:38,920
in its content.

407
00:17:39,119 --> 00:17:40,599
The content

408
00:17:40,599 --> 00:17:41,799
is also quite good.

409
00:17:42,599 --> 00:17:44,079
Santiago, the shepherd boy,

410
00:17:44,079 --> 00:17:45,240
crossed the entire continent

411
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:46,359
to find the treasure.

412
00:17:46,759 --> 00:17:48,359
On the way to pursuing his destiny,

413
00:17:48,359 --> 00:17:49,920
he learned to use all resources,

414
00:17:49,920 --> 00:17:51,039
persevered,

415
00:17:51,039 --> 00:17:52,799
and finally realized their own value.

416
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:56,880
Are you going to

417
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:58,920
read all the books on the list like this?

418
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:04,440
You'll find life in the desert,

419
00:18:05,359 --> 00:18:08,000
stars in the sky,

420
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:10,759
and soldiers fighting

421
00:18:10,759 --> 00:18:11,799
because war

422
00:18:11,799 --> 00:18:13,759
is part of human life.

423
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:17,160
Life is a festival,

424
00:18:18,039 --> 00:18:20,000
a grand celebration.

425
00:18:20,480 --> 00:18:22,480
Because life is

426
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:24,680
and will always be

427
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:26,920
the moment we are experiencing right now.

428
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:34,119
Don't remember, do you?

429
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:37,680
This is from the book.

430
00:18:38,559 --> 00:18:40,119
I've long noticed that

431
00:18:40,440 --> 00:18:42,279
for you, reading

432
00:18:42,279 --> 00:18:43,359
is just about completing the tasks

433
00:18:43,359 --> 00:18:44,880
your dad assigns to you.

434
00:18:45,640 --> 00:18:47,440
If we use travel as a metaphor,

435
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:49,880
you are the type who sleeps on the bus

436
00:18:49,880 --> 00:18:51,079
and checks in upon arrival,

437
00:18:51,240 --> 00:18:52,880
and complete tasks

438
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:54,759
with the help of AI.

439
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:57,960
But real reading

440
00:18:57,960 --> 00:18:59,039
isn't like that.

441
00:18:59,839 --> 00:19:00,559
You need to

442
00:19:00,559 --> 00:19:02,359
explore a whole new world,

443
00:19:03,240 --> 00:19:05,720
feel the wind and rain,

444
00:19:06,359 --> 00:19:09,200
and encounter all sorts of the unknown.

445
00:19:14,119 --> 00:19:14,799
Mom,

446
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:16,160
I'm sorry.

447
00:19:18,599 --> 00:19:19,839
You don't need

448
00:19:21,119 --> 00:19:22,119
to apologize to me

449
00:19:22,119 --> 00:19:23,680
for anything.

450
00:19:25,119 --> 00:19:26,279
I know

451
00:19:26,279 --> 00:19:27,720
your dad has always taught you

452
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:29,319
to be efficient.

453
00:19:30,559 --> 00:19:31,440
But I

454
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:33,240
still hope you can slow down,

455
00:19:33,799 --> 00:19:36,079
read a book,

456
00:19:36,519 --> 00:19:37,640
and take the time

457
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:39,200
to appreciate life.

458
00:19:40,079 --> 00:19:41,440
Maybe

459
00:19:41,759 --> 00:19:43,160
you'll be happier that way.

460
00:19:46,039 --> 00:19:47,279
Smile.

461
00:19:47,839 --> 00:19:48,400
Here,

462
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:51,400
have an orange.

463
00:19:53,720 --> 00:19:54,759
I won't bother you.

464
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:56,039
Take your time.

465
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:56,960
Okay.

466
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:38,359
Nice addition of an auxiliary line.

467
00:20:38,359 --> 00:20:39,279
Can you share

468
00:20:39,279 --> 00:20:40,359
how you thought of it?

469
00:20:40,799 --> 00:20:41,920
Zhou Yang came up with it.

470
00:20:42,279 --> 00:20:44,079
We discussed solutions yesterday.

471
00:20:44,359 --> 00:20:45,480
Very good.

472
00:20:45,480 --> 00:20:46,359
I'm looking forward

473
00:20:46,359 --> 00:20:47,640
to your good news in the next month's competition.

474
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:48,240
Okay.

475
00:20:48,640 --> 00:20:49,200
Go back.

476
00:20:50,279 --> 00:20:50,559
Okay.

477
00:20:50,559 --> 00:20:51,680
That's it for today's training.

478
00:20:51,680 --> 00:20:52,240
Class dismissed.

479
00:20:53,039 --> 00:20:54,359
Auxiliary line?

480
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:55,559
Who doesn't know that?

481
00:20:56,039 --> 00:20:57,359
Someone who doesn't even attend the training

482
00:20:57,359 --> 00:20:58,240
wants to win an award?

483
00:20:58,519 --> 00:20:59,440
That's funny.

484
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:01,240
Joining the training

485
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:02,680
is voluntary.

486
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:04,160
I came here

487
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:05,039
because I lack confidence.

488
00:21:05,559 --> 00:21:06,359
I didn't expect

489
00:21:07,119 --> 00:21:08,240
the level here to be even lower.

490
00:21:14,160 --> 00:21:15,200
Fu Binyan.

491
00:21:17,440 --> 00:21:18,200
Where's Zhou Yang?

492
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:20,920
He didn't come today.

493
00:21:20,920 --> 00:21:21,599
What's up?

494
00:21:22,039 --> 00:21:23,200
Is it about

495
00:21:23,400 --> 00:21:25,720
the Reading Week?

496
00:21:26,680 --> 00:21:28,000
Did he go

497
00:21:28,319 --> 00:21:29,119
tutor Li Haoyu

498
00:21:29,119 --> 00:21:30,079
and the others?

499
00:21:32,759 --> 00:21:34,200
I'll talk to

500
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:35,519
Ms. Wang again.

501
00:21:35,839 --> 00:21:37,000
As for Zhou Yang,

502
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,440
I'll leave it to you to remind him.

503
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:39,039
Okay.

504
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:53,160
[The spotlight burns the center of the]

505
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:56,640
[basketball court into a dazzling island.]

506
00:21:57,039 --> 00:21:58,480
[The deafening roar]

507
00:21:58,480 --> 00:22:01,920
[turns into a thick silence at this moment.]

508
00:22:02,279 --> 00:22:04,079
[I stand on the free-throw line,]

509
00:22:04,079 --> 00:22:05,920
[the white line beneath my feet]

510
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:09,480
[like a measure of fate.]

511
00:22:09,960 --> 00:22:12,079
Not bad, bro. A literary genius.

512
00:22:12,279 --> 00:22:13,319
Just a piece of cake.

513
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:18,680
Gu Chenyang,

514
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:19,880
what's the topic

515
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:20,720
of this essay?

516
00:22:21,039 --> 00:22:22,279
With the theme of facing,

517
00:22:22,279 --> 00:22:23,880
choose a familiar angle

518
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:26,240
to write a heartfelt essay.

519
00:22:26,240 --> 00:22:27,119
Keep reading.

520
00:22:27,119 --> 00:22:28,200
We're about to face it.

521
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:31,920
The score is tied.

522
00:22:31,920 --> 00:22:34,400
Time is running out.

523
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:36,640
The team's hope

524
00:22:36,640 --> 00:22:38,680
is on me,

525
00:22:39,039 --> 00:22:42,039
a 17-year-old defender.

526
00:22:47,200 --> 00:22:48,079
You're 17?

527
00:22:48,960 --> 00:22:49,880
AI wrote this, right?

528
00:22:49,880 --> 00:22:51,160
I just copied it.

529
00:22:51,599 --> 00:22:52,880
Who said this is AI?

530
00:22:53,319 --> 00:22:54,519
"A snow-bright island,

531
00:22:54,519 --> 00:22:55,759
a sticky silence,

532
00:22:55,759 --> 00:22:57,000
and the measure of fate."

533
00:22:57,640 --> 00:22:58,880
That's your writing style.

534
00:22:59,279 --> 00:23:00,799
I've known you for years.

535
00:23:00,799 --> 00:23:02,000
Who are you looking down on?

536
00:23:02,240 --> 00:23:03,160
Besides,

537
00:23:03,759 --> 00:23:04,559
don't you use AI

538
00:23:04,559 --> 00:23:05,279
every day?

539
00:23:05,480 --> 00:23:06,000
I use AI

540
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,240
as a learning tool,

541
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:08,720
not to do my work for me.

542
00:23:09,039 --> 00:23:09,599
Besides,

543
00:23:09,599 --> 00:23:10,440
during exams,

544
00:23:10,440 --> 00:23:11,559
can AI help you?

545
00:23:12,599 --> 00:23:13,720
Enough, enough.

546
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:14,799
Let's check mine out.

547
00:23:17,599 --> 00:23:18,880
Speaking of facing,

548
00:23:18,880 --> 00:23:20,440
Lu Xun once said,

549
00:23:20,680 --> 00:23:21,799
a true hero

550
00:23:21,799 --> 00:23:24,279
dares to face a bleak life

551
00:23:24,279 --> 00:23:26,559
and the bloodshed.

552
00:23:26,559 --> 00:23:28,400
Franklin Roosevelt said,

553
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:30,400
face the things you fear

554
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:31,680
and go forward.

555
00:23:32,960 --> 00:23:34,480
Charles de Gaulle said...

556
00:23:35,079 --> 00:23:36,559
Bi Shumin said...

557
00:23:36,880 --> 00:23:38,519
Einstein also said...

558
00:23:40,480 --> 00:23:41,680
What's this?

559
00:23:41,680 --> 00:23:43,039
Just tell me if it's correct

560
00:23:43,039 --> 00:23:44,359
and on topic.

561
00:23:44,640 --> 00:23:45,240
Are you using the composition paper

562
00:23:45,240 --> 00:23:46,359
as a school corridor?

563
00:23:46,359 --> 00:23:47,640
It's all quotes from famous people.

564
00:23:48,759 --> 00:23:49,799
I don't have AI.

565
00:23:49,799 --> 00:23:51,000
I searched for these quotes myself

566
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:52,160
and copied them by hand.

567
00:23:52,160 --> 00:23:53,839
Can you copy during exams?

568
00:24:01,880 --> 00:24:02,880
When writing essays,

569
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:04,920
the most important thing is genuine feelings.

570
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:06,880
AI may have a fancy way with words,

571
00:24:07,359 --> 00:24:08,559
but it's too hollow.

572
00:24:08,880 --> 00:24:10,000
Famous quotes

573
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:10,839
may make sense,

574
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:11,960
but they can't replace

575
00:24:11,960 --> 00:24:13,400
our true feelings.

576
00:24:13,839 --> 00:24:15,920
You two, rewrite an essay now.

577
00:24:16,359 --> 00:24:19,119
About the last basketball game loss.

578
00:24:19,119 --> 00:24:20,240
No, no.

579
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:21,839
We've lost the game.

580
00:24:21,839 --> 00:24:22,920
Why do we have to write it?

581
00:24:23,359 --> 00:24:25,240
This is called facing.

582
00:24:25,519 --> 00:24:26,200
Do you understand?

583
00:24:29,240 --> 00:24:30,240
Okay, okay.

584
00:24:30,240 --> 00:24:31,440
Let's think about it.

585
00:24:34,480 --> 00:24:35,319
All right.

586
00:24:35,319 --> 00:24:37,160
I'll go buy you something to eat.

587
00:24:37,200 --> 00:24:37,839
Come on.

588
00:24:43,720 --> 00:24:44,599
Hello, mom.

589
00:24:44,960 --> 00:24:46,880
I didn't go out with my classmates.

590
00:24:46,920 --> 00:24:48,680
I was reading in the classroom.

591
00:24:48,799 --> 00:24:49,599
I'll be back soon.

592
00:24:49,599 --> 00:24:50,240
Bin Yan

593
00:24:52,400 --> 00:24:53,359
Why are you here?

594
00:24:53,920 --> 00:24:55,599
The Olympiad mathematics contest is coming.

595
00:24:55,599 --> 00:24:57,200
You still have time to set up a study group.

596
00:24:57,519 --> 00:24:58,480
It's okay.

597
00:24:58,480 --> 00:24:59,680
I've arranged my time.

598
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:01,000
It won't delay the contest.

599
00:25:01,759 --> 00:25:03,200
You have limited energy.

600
00:25:03,400 --> 00:25:04,720
You may have made a schedule,

601
00:25:05,039 --> 00:25:06,400
but can your body

602
00:25:06,839 --> 00:25:08,000
handle it?

603
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:10,799
Don't worry. I know what I'm doing.

604
00:25:12,079 --> 00:25:14,759
Why hasn't Zhou Yang come back?

605
00:25:15,960 --> 00:25:16,880
Do you need help?

606
00:25:17,400 --> 00:25:18,000
No, thanks.

607
00:25:18,480 --> 00:25:19,160
You also need to

608
00:25:19,160 --> 00:25:20,240
prepare for the Olympiad.

609
00:25:23,240 --> 00:25:23,839
Well.

610
00:25:24,079 --> 00:25:25,920
It's the business of Basketball Club.

611
00:25:25,920 --> 00:25:27,119
We can handle it ourselves.

612
00:25:27,359 --> 00:25:28,359
Go back early.

613
00:25:28,640 --> 00:25:29,480
I'm going in.

614
00:25:30,440 --> 00:25:31,079
Bye.

615
00:25:32,160 --> 00:25:32,920
I'm back.

616
00:25:34,279 --> 00:25:35,640
Why are you just back?

617
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:38,079
What did you buy?
